1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:06,680
Nine a.m. Emails, Slack, invites, DSP exports, product updates…

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,540
By eleven, we are still catching up.

3
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:16,840
Everything we need is in there. No one can read it all.

4
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:22,200
So we built J.A.R.V.I.S., the AI co-pilot of the PSC.

5
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:26,200
It reads everything: mail, Slack, calendar, DSP exports, tickets, docs.

6
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:32,460
It knows what matters. And it does the work. One brain. One platform.

7
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:36,840
Every morning, ninety emails become three lines.

8
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:50,380
Every DSP export is read. Under-delivery is caught first, and becomes a costed task.

9
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:02,240
It writes like me, grounded in live data. I add a note in French: it rewrites it.

10
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:10,480
A dedicated agent preps every meeting the day before.

11
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:19,080
One sentence: the deck and the WBR are ready.

12
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:28,260
And everything else lives in the same platform.

13
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:37,660
Add it up: eight hours back, every week. One working day per PSC.

14
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:42,300
We stay in control: nothing is ever sent on its own.

15
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:46,900
And it learns from every email, document and campaign result.

16
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:51,480
Next: Salesforce, then connected brains for the whole team.

17
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:54,080
Stop searching. Start consulting.

18
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:56,160
This is J.A.R.V.I.S.
